    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/head-men-and-womens-tennis-coach-part-time/": {
      "title": "Head Men and Women’s Tennis Coach (Part-time, Seasonal)",
      "description": "Head Men and Women's Tennis Coach (Part-time, Seasonal) - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Head Men and Women’s Tennis Coach (Part-time, Seasonal) Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Head Men and Women’s Tennis Coach (Part-time, Seasonal) Head Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach (Part-Time, Seasonal) Reports To: Director of Athletics Position Summary Chestnut Hill College seeks an enthusiastic, student-centered leader to serve as the Head Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach for its NCAA Division II athletics program. This part-time, seasonal position provides an exciting opportunity to lead and grow two competitive tennis programs while mentoring student-athletes in their athletic, academic, and personal development. Working closely with the Director of Athletics, the Head Coach is responsible for the overall leadership, administration, and operation of the men’s and women’s tennis programs, including recruiting, player development, practice and competition planning, program administration, and compliance with NCAA, Central Atlantic Collegiate Conference (CACC), and College policies. The successful candidate will foster a culture of integrity, sportsmanship, academic excellence, and competitive success while supporting the mission and values of Chestnut Hill College. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition and committed to educating the whole person. The College provides a welcoming, mission-driven environment that values academic excellence, service, leadership, and inclusion. Located in the historic Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, the College serves a diverse student population and competes as a proud member of NCAA Division II and the Central Atlantic Collegiate Conference (CACC). Qualifications Required: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Minimum of two years of coaching experience at the high school, collegiate, club, or comparable competitive level. Demonstrated knowledge of tennis instruction, player development, training techniques, and match strategy. Strong organizational, leadership, and interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to mentoring and supporting student-athletes academically, athletically, and personally. Demonstrated integrity, professionalism, and ethical conduct consistent with the mission and values of Chestnut Hill College. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required. Preferred: Master’s degree. Collegiate coaching and recruiting experience. Knowledge of NCAA Division II and CACC rules and regulations. Essential Responsibilities The Head Coach is responsible for the overall leadership and administration of the men’s and women’s tennis programs, including: Recruit, evaluate, and retain qualified student-athletes in collaboration with the Offices of Admissions and Athletics. Plan, organize, and conduct practices, conditioning sessions, competitions, and player development activities. Foster a positive team culture that emphasizes academic achievement, sportsmanship, leadership, and personal growth. Supervise, mentor, and evaluate assistant coach(es). Develop competitive schedules in collaboration with the Assistant Athletic Director. Assist with the purchasing and management of team equipment, uniforms, and supplies. Ensure compliance with all NCAA, CACC, College, and departmental rules, policies, and procedures, including the timely completion of all required NCAA coaching education modules. Monitor student-athletes’ academic progress and promote academic success by coordinating team activities around class schedules and examinations. Maintain appropriate standards of conduct for student-athletes during practices, competitions, team travel, and all College-related activities. Represent Chestnut Hill College with professionalism and integrity while building positive relationships with prospective student-athletes, families, alumni, officials, opponents, faculty, staff, and supporters. Attend departmental, conference, and NCAA meetings as required. Coordinate annual team awards and recognition activities. Maintain current CPR, AED, and First Aid certifications. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Why Join Chestnut Hill College? At Chestnut Hill College, coaches are educators, mentors, and leaders. You will have the opportunity to make a lasting impact on the lives of student-athletes while building competitive NCAA Division II tennis programs within a supportive, mission-driven athletic department. Contact Information: Application Process Interested candidates should submit application materials via ADP Workforce Now HERE. No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Head Men and Women’s Tennis Coach (Part-time, Seasonal) Associate Registrar Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Head Men and Women's Tennis Coach (Part-time, Seasonal) Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Assistant Professor/Field Placement Coordinator (MCCP) Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Maternal Child Health (OB Fall 2026) Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Megan Fox Playoff Appearances Abound in Historic Year... Chestnut Hill College to Add Women’s Flag..."
    },
    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/undergraduate-admissions-counselor/": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Undergraduate Admissions Counselor - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Position: Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Reports to: Associate Director of Undergraduate Admissions Department: Undergraduate Admissions Position Summary: The Undergraduate Admissions Counselor serves as a key ambassador for the College, guiding prospective students and families through the admissions process with professionalism, enthusiasm, and care. This role focuses on building meaningful connections, sharing the value of the College’s academic and campus experience, and supporting students from initial inquiry through enrollment. The Counselor represents the institution at recruitment events, both in-person and virtually, and plays an active role in shaping a diverse and engaged incoming class. Success in this position requires strong communication, relationship-building, and problem-solving skills, as well as the ability to think strategically and manage a dynamic schedule that includes travel and participation in events during peak recruitment seasons. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition that fosters equality through holistic education. Distinguished by its strong mission, collegial environment, and dedication to personalized instruction through a small faculty-to-student ratio, the College promotes the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. Located in the charming Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, CHC serves a culturally diverse student body. Duties & Responsibilities: Manage all activities related to prospective students, applicants, school districts, and colleges from a specific territory/population Attend regional and national college fairs (virtual where applicable) Report on recruitment initiatives, including tracking of inquiries, applications, follow-up contacts, campus visits, etc. that allow for the analysis of enrollment strategies Conduct engagement via telephone, email, written, and personal contact with prospective students, families, and school personnel Conduct file review and information sessions for all populations. Provide campus tours when needed. Promptly respond to phone calls, emails and inquiries Conduct weekly call campaigns and meet high-volume weekly call goals Manage application flow. Evaluate admissions applications and make admission decisions or recommendations in a timely fashion. Assist the financial aid office by providing support during peak times. Work closely with other campus offices to provide information students need to convert acceptances to enrollments Assist with the planning of enrollment related events such as Open House, Admitted Student Days, Group Tours, etc. Extensive travel is required for in-person recruitment to targeted schools, colleges and events in assigned regions to provide presentations to students and parents, including evening and weekend programs. Frequent evening and weekend availability are required. Peak travel seasons: fall and spring. Coordinate special projects as assigned Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college/university. Prior customer service experience Excellent oral and written communication abilities. Engage positively and professionally with diverse groups, fostering strong relationships with prospective students, families, colleagues, and stakeholders. Effectively sell the institution’s value amid higher education difficulties. Proven ability to prioritize multiple tasks, manage deadlines, and stay organized while balancing travel and recruitment duties. Comfortable presenting to large audiences both in-person and virtually. Handle sensitive information with discretion. Meet recruitment targets and deadlines while performing duties off campus (traveling to recruitment events). Strong critical thinking, creativity, and strategic decision-making skills demonstrated through effectively identifying and resolving challenges. Must possess a valid driver’s license, reliable transportation, and car insurance. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Contact Information: Application Process Interested candidates should submit application materials via ADP Workforce Now HERE. No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Associate Registrar Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Head Men and Women's Tennis Coach (Part-time, Seasonal) Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Assistant Professor/Field Placement Coordinator (MCCP) Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Maternal Child Health (OB Fall 2026) Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Employment Opportunities Financial Aid Counselor Undergraduate Admissions Team"
